  "description": "PEWXEY crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C108 H120 Ce6 O36,6(C4 H8 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce1B (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce2B (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce3B (Ce) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.760-3.871 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.67-121.39°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula Ce6O4(OH)4(O2CC8H9)12(OH2)4 (C108H120Ce6O36). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(V).",
